`qualifier` keyword argument. The tests call it as `proverb(*items, qualifier=...)` and expect a list of lines back.\n\n- **Chain verses:** pair each item with the next one using `zip(inputs, inputs[1:])` to build the \"For want of a X the Y was lost.\" lines.\n- **Final verse:** \"And all for the want of a ...\" uses the first item. If a `qualifier` is given, it goes in front of that item (e.g. \"horseshoe nail\").\n- **Empty input:** return an empty list.\n\nproverb.py\n```python\ndef proverb(*inputs, qualifier=None):\n    \"\"\"Generate the proverbial rhyme for the given chain of inputs.\n\n    :param inputs: str - the items in the chain, in order of consequence.\n    :param qualifier: str or None - optional word used to modify the first\n                      item in the final verse (e.g. \"horseshoe\" -> \"horseshoe nail\").\n    :return: list[str] - the lines of the proverb.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not inputs:\n        return []\n\n    verses = [\n        f\"For want of a {wanted} the {lost} was lost.\"\n        for wanted, lost in zip(inputs, inputs[1:])\n    ]\n\n    first, *_ = inputs\n    subject = f\"{qualifier} {first}\" if qualifier else first\n    verses.append(f\"And all for the want of a {subject}.\")\n\n    return verses\n```", "blocks": [{"index": 0, "type": "thinking", "chars": 0, "signature": true}, {"index": 1, "type": "text", "chars": 1272, "signature": false}], "events": 85, "event_types": {"message_start": 1, "content_block_start": 2, "ping": 1, "content_block_delta": 77, "content_block_stop": 2, "message_delta": 1, "message_stop": 1}}
